{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-447493-r4518663","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Obe Eja Kika (Nigerian Smoked Fish Stew)","sourcePageId":447493,"sourceRevision":"4518663","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:31:37Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Obe%20Eja%20Kika%20(Nigerian%20Smoked%20Fish%20Stew)&oldid=4518663","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:41.963Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for stew","Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth","Category:Recipes using fish","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using habanero chile","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using red bell pepper","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Yoruba recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"539e8903adc96bc814a137d2d2543f43a44ede62841a391b068b70723e12e631","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Stew recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Obe eja kika''' is a Nigerian [[Cookbook:Stew|stew]] of smoked panla (hake) fish. In Nigeria, this fish can be used to prepare any type of dish that requires the use of fish. This fish is mostly used by the Yoruba people of Nigeria.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* Fresh, hard [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* Fresh habanero pepper (ata rodo)\n* 5 large red [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|tatashe peppers]]\n* 2 green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]] (optional)\n* About 3 big [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Palm Oil|palm oil]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] fish powder\n* Shrimp seasoning powder\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Stock Cube|Stock cube]]\n* Smoked [[Cookbook:Panla|panla]] fish, cleaned\n* [[Cookbook:Scent Leaf|Scent leaf]] (nchawu effirin)\n\n==Procedure==\n# Coarsely grind the tomatoes, habanero pepper, tatashe, green bell peppers, and onions.\n# Heat the palm oil and vegetable oil in a pot. Add the ground pepper mix, and cook, stirring, for about 10–15 minutes.\n# Stir in the fish seasoning powder, shrimp powder, salt, and stock cube. Add the panla fish, and stir.\n# Add some water to loosen up the stew, stir, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] for 10–15 minutes on low heat.\n# Stir in the scent leaf, and remove from the heat.\n# Serve with rice, pasta, or boiled yam.\n\n[[Category:Yoruba recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using habanero chile]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Obe Eja Kika (Nigerian Smoked Fish Stew)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Fresh, hard tomatoes","sourceText":"Fresh, hard tomatoes","amountText":"Fresh, hard tomatoes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Fresh habanero pepp